// Indexes — curated landing pages mirroring the structure of the original wdoc
// section of the WCL reference book: the core document/content chapters, with the
// "Diagrams" sub-section nested as a child index. `documents` is a top-level book
// menu entry; `diagrams_section` renders nested beneath it (book TOC + skill list).

index documents {
  name    = "Documents & Content"
  summary = "The core wdoc chapters: the document model (pages, sites, render targets) and the content blocks that fill a page."
  audience = :both
  body {
    p "This mirrors the **wdoc** section of the reference (everything before the Diagrams sub-section) — how a document is structured and what goes on a page."

    h2 "The document model"
    p "Start with the [overview](concept_overview), then the pieces: [Sites & Templates](concept_sites), [Pages](concept_pages), [Including sub-sites](concept_includes), [Block Visibility](concept_visibility), [Markdown Output](concept_markdown) and [Skill Folders](concept_skills). The built-in [template kinds](fact_template_kinds) and [themes](fact_themes) set the output shape and palette."

    h2 "Content blocks"
    p "What fills a page: [Formatting](concept_formatting) and the text [primitives](concept_primitives) — headings, paragraphs and code — plus [Tables](entity_tables_block), [lists](entity_lists_block), [callouts](entity_callouts), [Columns](concept_columns), [Math Equations](entity_math), [Icons](entity_icons), [Images](entity_images) and [Videos](entity_videos). The [callout classes](fact_callout_classes) list the admonition styles."

    h2 "Data & styling"
    p "Project content from a typed model with [Data Views](concept_data_views) (repeaters, components, bodies), and theme it with [Styling](concept_styling)."
  }

  // Nested sub-index — renders beneath "Documents & Content" in both projections.
  index diagrams_section {
    name    = "Diagrams"
    summary = "The diagram family: the SVG canvas, the auto-layout modes, and every higher-level shape — graphs, charts, maps, sprites, terminals and wireframes."
    audience = :both
    body {
      p "This mirrors the nested **Diagrams** sub-section of the reference. Everything here lives inside a [diagram](entity_diagrams) canvas, built from [primitive shapes](concept_primitives) and wired with [connections](concept_connections); the [layout modes](fact_layout_modes) place shapes automatically."

      h2 "Graphs & flow"
      p "[Flowcharts](entity_flowcharts), [sequence diagrams](entity_sequence_diagrams), [state diagrams](entity_state_diagrams) and [trees](entity_tree) turn a connection graph into a ranked, routed picture."

      h2 "Data visualisation"
      p "[Charts](entity_charts) (bar / line / pie) and [timelines](entity_timelines) plot values directly from WCL data."

      h2 "Grids & sprites"
      p "[Tilemaps](entity_tilemaps), [dopesheets](entity_dopesheets) and [maps](entity_maps) lay out tiled, animated, or pinned content."

      h2 "Terminal & UI"
      p "[Terminals](entity_terminals) render an ANSI grid; [wireframes](entity_wireframe) mock up UI with `wf_*` widgets."
    }
  }
}
